        "username": "Thunderbird",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/ba8739/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2021-09-29T01:46:51.360Z",
        "cooked": "<p><div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/original/2X/d/da06ba79912bc05c0d38a956b267cc18eab00b93.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/da06ba79912bc05c0d38a956b267cc18eab00b93\" title=\"20210928202949_1\"><img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/d/da06ba79912bc05c0d38a956b267cc18eab00b93_2_690x431.jpeg\" alt=\"20210928202949_1\" data-base62-sha1=\"v6KvfRiFtMlM2LyAY46Tith1hAL\" width=\"690\" height=\"431\" srcset=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/d/da06ba79912bc05c0d38a956b267cc18eab00b93_2_690x431.jpeg, https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/d/da06ba79912bc05c0d38a956b267cc18eab00b93_2_1035x646.jpeg 1.5x, https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/d/da06ba79912bc05c0d38a956b267cc18eab00b93_2_1380x862.jpeg 2x\" data-small-upload=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/d/da06ba79912bc05c0d38a956b267cc18eab00b93_2_10x10.png\"><div class=\"meta\">\n<svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use xlink:href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\">20210928202949_1</span><span class=\"informations\">1680×1050 321 KB</span><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use xlink:href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg>\n</div></a></div></p>\n<p>Yeah, not too bad. Did as others said, just let him keep the Catastrophes out until he flips. He only wiped out 1 environment card that way, so the heroes just barely pinged themselves before he hit for 4 each. Much better than what I was about to do, play Emergency Evac on his front side and take out two Catastrophes. That would’ve hurt me much worse than him! Dark Visionary synced nicely with normal size Skyscraper, and let her set up the bottom card play each time. Chrono Ranger with an Ultimate Target and Compounded Bow became even more deadly when By Any Means came out. IIRC, Deadline went down the next turn with an Explosive Reveal by Skyscraper leading to a Colossal Left Hook off the bottom of her deck.</p>",
